(There are many times where we want to do an operation to every entry in \a vector or matrix. Matlab will )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(allow you to do this with "element-wise" operations. For example, suppos\e you want to multiply each )Tj
T*
(entry in vector v with its cooresponding entry in vector b. In other wor\ds, suppose you want to find v\(1\)*b)Tj
T*
(\(1\), v\(2\)*b\(2\), and v\(3\)*b\(3\). It would be nice to use the "*"\ symbol since you are doing some sort of )Tj
T*
(multiplication, but since it already has a definition, we have to come u\p with something else. The )Tj
T*
(programmers who came up with Matlab decided to use the symbols ".*" to d\o this. In fact, you can put a )Tj
T*
(period in front of any math symbol to tell Matlab that you want the oper\ation to take place on each entry of )Tj
T*
(the vector. )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
