(The ability to work with these vector functions is one of the advantages\ of Matlab. Now complex )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(operations can be defined that can be done quickly and easily. In the fo\llowing example a very large vector )Tj
T*
(is defined and can be easily manipulated. \(Notice that the second comma\nd has a ";" at the end of the line. )Tj
T*
(This tells Matlab that it should not print out the result.\) )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> x = [0:0.1:100])Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(x =)Tj
T*
(  Columns 1 through 7 )Tj
T*
(         0    0.1000    0.2000    0.3000    0.4000    0.5000    0.6000)Tj
T*
(    [stuff deleted])Tj
