0 -3.60001 TD
(>> y = sin\(x\).*x./\(1+cos\(x\)\);)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
0 -3.75233 TD
(Through this simple manipulation of vectors, Matlab will also let you gr\aph the results. The following )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(example also demonstrates one of the most useful commands in Matlab, the\ "help" command. )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
0 -2.56197 TD
(>> plot\(x,y\))Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(>> plot\(x,y,'rx'\))Tj
T*
(>> help plot)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
( PLOT   Linear plot. )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    PLOT\(X,Y\) plots vector Y versus vector X. If X or Y is a matrix,)Tj
T*
(    then the vector is plotted versus the rows or columns of the matrix,\)Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
(    whichever line up.  If X is a scalar and Y is a vector, length\(Y\))Tj
