/T1_1 1 Tf
11.08206 0 0 11.08206 122.17265 758.09578 Tm
(    disconnected points are plotted.)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
( )Tj
T*
(    PLOT\(Y\) plots the columns of Y versus their index.)Tj
T*
(    If Y is complex, PLOT\(Y\) is equivalent to PLOT\(real\(Y\),imag\(Y\)\\).)Tj
T*
(    In all other uses of PLOT, the imaginary part is ignored.)Tj
T*
( )Tj
T*
(    Various line types, plot symbols and colors may be obtained with)Tj
T*
(    PLOT\(X,Y,S\) where S is a character string made from one element)Tj
T*
(    from any or all the following 3 columns:)Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
( )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(           b     blue          .     point              -     solid)Tj
T*
(           g     green         o     circle             :     dotted)Tj
T*
(           r     red           x     x-mark             -.    dashdot )Tj
T*
(           c     cyan          +     plus               --    dashed   )Tj
T*
(           m     magenta       *     star)Tj
T*
(           y     yellow        s     square)Tj
T*
(           k     black         d     diamond)Tj
T*
(                               v     triangle \(down\))Tj
T*
(                               ^     triangle \(up\))Tj
T*
(                               <     triangle \(left\))Tj
T*
(                               >     triangle \(right\))Tj
T*
(                               p     pentagram)Tj
T*
(                               h     hexagram)Tj
T*
(                          )Tj
T*
(    For example, PLOT\(X,Y,'c+:'\) plots a cyan dotted line with a plus \)Tj
T*
(    at each data point; PLOT\(X,Y,'bd'\) plots blue diamond at each data\ )Tj
T*
(    point but does not draw any line.)Tj
T*
( )Tj
T*
(    PLOT\(X1,Y1,S1,X2,Y2,S2,X3,Y3,S3,...\) combines the plots defined by\)Tj
T*
(    the \(X,Y,S\) triples, where the X's and Y's are vectors or matrices\ )Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
(    and the S's are strings.  )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
( )Tj
T*
(    For example, PLOT\(X,Y,'y-',X,Y,'go'\) plots the data twice, with a)Tj
T*
(    solid yellow line interpolating green circles at the data points.)Tj
T*
( )Tj
T*
(    The PLOT command, if no color is specified, makes automatic use of)Tj
T*
(    the colors specified by the axes ColorOrder property.  The default)Tj
T*
(    ColorOrder is listed in the table above for color systems where the)Tj
T*
(    default is blue for one line, and for multiple lines, to cycle)Tj
T*
(    through the first six colors in the table.  For monochrome systems,)Tj
T*
(    PLOT cycles over the axes LineStyleOrder property.)Tj
T*
( )Tj
T*
(    PLOT returns a column vector of handles to LINE objects, one)Tj
T*
(    handle per line. )Tj
T*
( )Tj
T*
(    The X,Y pairs, or X,Y,S triples, can be followed by )Tj
T*
(    parameter/value pairs to specify additional properties )Tj
T*
(    of the lines.)Tj
T*
(                                    )Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
(    See also SEMILOGX, SEMILOGY, LOGLOG, PLOTYY, GRID, CLF, CLC, TITLE,)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    XLABEL, YLABEL, AXIS, AXES, HOLD, COLORDEF, LEGEND, SUBPLOT, STEM.)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
( Overloaded methods)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(    help idmodel/plot.m)Tj
T*
(    help iddata/plot.m)Tj
ET
